==== 3b. Limits found while building the cases ====
  39 g, step 11 -> 11.5 mm from hover: overshoot 0.42 mm, lowest point 11.92 mm, stand at 11.92 mm -> TOUCHES THE STAND
  42 g, step 11 -> 11.5 mm from hover: overshoot 0.42 mm, lowest point 11.92 mm, stand at 11.92 mm -> TOUCHES THE STAND
  Lab (Exp A, 39 g, same step): overshoot 0.33-0.34 mm, closest 0.11 mm to the stand reading (contact not
  excluded). Within ~0.8 mm of the stand the model lacks the stand-proximity effect (16-Nov README), so this
  comparison lies outside the model's range. 11.5 mm (normal stand) is outside the claimed range.
  kg 0.4, ball on the stand: steady coil current 0.925 A (integral clamped) vs 0.939 A needed to lift -> cannot lift; sim: no lift in 3 s
PASS: static hand calculation and simulation agree on lift-off at kg = 0.4
